  "scope": "Supported: 14..30 grids; 1-3 solid rectangular frames; 1-4 holes per frame. Holes are single rectangles, 2-3 rectangles stacked along a full edge, or two rectangles joined along part of an edge (L/T/step). Each hole rectangle becomes one loose rectangular piece with a random colour that differs from its host frame. Colours repeat freely, as in the fixtures. There are 3-12 grey noise singletons. Not supported: non-rectangular pieces, rotated fits, unused distractor pieces, non-rectangular frames, and holes that a piece could only fill after rotation. Requested width/height are honored. Random frame sides extend to 18, supporting tall frames like the originals.",
  "constraints": [
    "Holes lie strictly inside their frame. Different holes are separated by at least one frame cell, including diagonally.",
    "Frames, pieces and noise cells are pairwise non-touching (8-neighbourhood gap). This keeps components distinct and prevents accidental enclosed background.",
    "A piece's colour never equals its host frame's colour.",
    "Total piece area equals total hole area. Every piece is used, and every frame has at least one hole.",
    "A local exact-cover enumerator (translations only) must find exactly one distinct coloured filling; otherwise the scene is resampled.",
    "Background 0 is strictly the most frequent input colour.",
    "Fixtures are rebuilt from explicit frames, pieces (src/dst) and noise latents."
  ],
  "known_limitations": [
    "Pieces are always solid rectangles, matching the fixtures.",
    "Rejection sampling (bounded at 600 attempts) is used for layout fit and tiling uniqueness. A RuntimeError is raised if every attempt fails, which should be rare.",
    "Each hole's internal decomposition gives its piece set exactly. The uniqueness check only accepts scenes whose coloured result is forced across all holes.",
    "No unused distractor pieces are generated. The task's accounting requires piece area equal to hole area."
  ],
